// expect: 7
// SYNTAX §«Equality operator» — a product compares "field-wise recursion
// over the sorted field set", so two records differing in ANY field are
// unequal. Both fields are named in the annotation here, which closes the
// row and makes the full set knowable.
//
// The contract is discriminating on purpose: a correct comparison answers
// false and exits 7, a comparison that found them equal exits 1.
//
// Its open-row twin is a MEASURED SILENT WRONG and is held back with its
// fix: replace `y: Int` below with `...` and the same call answers TRUE,
// because the comparison walks only the fields the type knows
// (`Hβ.fold.open-record-shares-closed-signature`). Both readings were
// taken before this fixture was written.
fn same(a: {x: Int, y: Int}, b: {x: Int, y: Int}) = a == b

fn main() = if same({x: 1, y: 2}, {x: 1, y: 3}) {
  1
} else {
  7
}
